{"id":2419,"date":"2021-01-21T11:12:45","date_gmt":"2021-01-21T19:12:45","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=2419"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:41:33","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:41:33","slug":"device-setup","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/device-setup\/","title":{"rendered":"Device Setup"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22166639675\" name=\"6a22166639675\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Checklist<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This lesson will go over the following steps:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install latest Python release (v3.7 or above)<\/li>\n<li>Install PyCharm Edu<\/li>\n<li>Set up PyCharm Edu for CoDrone Mini<\/li>\n<li>Run the test program<\/li>\n<li>Label your micro USB cable<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>If you have any trouble completing these steps throughout the lesson, please reach out to us on the <a href=\"https:\/\/forum.robolink.com\/\">forum<\/a> so that we can help you get started![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22166639789\" name=\"6a22166639789\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Python Installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Install Python on your Mac or Windows machine. If you\u2019re using a guest or limited account, <strong>m<\/strong><strong>ake sure you have access to admin credentials<\/strong> for installing new software on the computer. This is especially important for students using a school computer or parent computer with limited access. If you\u2019re on a Mac computer, you may need to modify the security settings in system preferences in order to download software.<\/p>\n<p>Click <a href=\"https:\/\/www.python.org\/\">here<\/a> to go to the Python website and download Python.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/7iy3MRC9eys&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Mac Installation Video&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/uAHbtxUkMV8&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Windows Installation&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221666397e6\" name=\"6a221666397e6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>PyCharm Edu Installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next, install PyCharm Edu, which is what we&#8217;ll use for writing out our Python code and running it on CoDrone Mini.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Note: <\/strong>If you choose not to use PyCharm and prefer your own editor or IDE, you will need to know how to install packages on your platform of choice. If you are not sure how to do this, we recommend installing PyCharm and following the next step to see how to install the library.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/VOC6NqVjGhM&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Mac Installation&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/ZC3bY5BNzQI&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Windows Installation&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22166639847\" name=\"6a22166639847\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Set up PyCharm Edu<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To use CoDrone Mini with PyCharm, you will need to open a new project with the right environment and install the CoDrone Mini library. Follow the videos below to get started.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/JlDhgf9HXkA&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Mac Setup&#8221;][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/yTh_fT5sSeM&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Windows Setup&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221666398a5\" name=\"6a221666398a5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Test Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To make sure you have everything installed, let&#8217;s run a test program. First, connect your controller to your controller and power on your CoDrone Mini.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]Now you are going to run a simple test code that will make your drone take off, hover, and land. Copy and paste the following code into a new file and run the program. Make sure you have enough space! If you have trouble pairing, move on to the next step.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">import CoDrone_mini\r\n\r\ndrone = CoDrone_mini.CoDrone()\r\ndrone.pair()\r\n\r\ndrone.takeoff()\r\ndrone.hover(3)\r\ndrone.land()<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/vS-g_sfSIkE&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221; title=&#8221;Test Program Video Walkthrough&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221666398fb\" name=\"6a221666398fb\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Driver Installation<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you were able to pair successfully in the last step, you can skip the driver installation. Some devices will not recognize the CoDrone Mini controller so you will need to download a driver. You can download the driver below for your device:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1a2NPQoyjvr8hwWxO1I5T-ZFowznYsx9E\/view\">Download MacOS Driver<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1ge1JZaClAL1ERtx7ATJFxvAFaHGX8VBM\/view\">Download Windows Driver<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:<\/strong> The drivers for CoDrone Mini and CoDrone Lite\/Pro are <strong>different<\/strong>. Make sure you install from the links above if you are using CoDrone Mini.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22166639941\" name=\"6a22166639941\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Label your microUSB cable<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Mark the USB cable that came in the package with a tape\u2014choose something obvious, like a colorful tape. This is because some USB cables only provide power but don\u2019t transfer data, so you\u2019ll want to distinguish it from others.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2434&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22166639985\" name=\"6a22166639985\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>All done!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You are ready to start learning Python with CoDrone Mini! Click the next lesson to get started. Please leave any feedback or issues you had on our <a href=\"http:\/\/forum.robolink.com\">forum<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Checklist [vc_column_text]This lesson will go over the following steps: Install latest Python release (v3.7 or above) Install PyCharm Edu Set up PyCharm Edu for CoDrone Mini Run&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/device-setup\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2426,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":744,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2125,2177,2134],"class_list":["post-2419","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-getting-started","lesson-tag-python","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2419","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2419\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2766,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/2419\/revisions\/2766"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/2426"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2419"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=2419"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=2419"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}